WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:26.394
One afternoon, Nello and Patrasche had finished delivering the milk, and once more, Patrasche was watching outside the gates of the cathedral.

2
00:00:26.395 --> 00:00:30.555
Patrasche noticed the church guard leave.

3
00:00:30.556 --> 00:00:37.017
He crept through the gates, up to the cathedral's open doors, and inside.

4
00:00:37.018 --> 00:00:44.059
In the dark church, he saw Nello kneeling down and staring at the high altar.

5
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:50.093
On it was the painting of the Assumption by Rubens.

6
00:00:50.094 --> 00:00:57.181
On the walls of the cathedral, on either side of the altar, were two more paintings.

7
00:00:57.182 --> 00:01:00.785
But each was covered by a curtain.

8
00:01:00.786 --> 00:01:06.684
Patrasche saw two wealthy gentlemen put money in a metal box.

9
00:01:06.685 --> 00:01:11.774
Then, they went behind the curtain to see one of the paintings.

10
00:01:11.775 --> 00:01:18.363
Nello noticed Patrasche, went over to him, and took him gently outside.

11
00:01:18.364 --> 00:01:22.717
He looked back at the veiled paintings as they left.

12
00:01:22.718 --> 00:01:26.032
His face was wet with tears.

13
00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:35.654
"It's terrible I can't see them, Patrasche," he said, "just because I'm poor!

14
00:01:35.655 --> 00:01:41.931
I'm sure Rubens thought everybody should see his paintings!" Nello said.

15
00:01:41.932 --> 00:01:45.912
"But those two paintings are behind curtains!

16
00:01:45.913 --> 00:01:49.872
No one sees them except rich people.

17
00:01:49.873 --> 00:01:55.652
If I could only see them, I would die a happy person."

18
00:01:55.653 --> 00:02:00.276
It was true that Nello's little family was poor.

19
00:02:00.277 --> 00:02:05.805
Any extra money was used to buy firewood or more food.

20
00:02:05.806 --> 00:02:13.848
Nello longed to see the two veiled paintings, and Patrasche knew he could do nothing to help.

21
00:02:13.849 --> 00:02:16.897
The little boy loved art.

22
00:02:16.898 --> 00:02:25.345
When Nello stood before the altar painting in Antwerp's cathedral, he felt as if he were in heaven.

23
00:02:25.346 --> 00:02:32.201
The glory of the great master's art made his heart stir with joy.

24
00:02:32.202 --> 00:02:36.111
Nello drew with whatever he could find.

25
00:02:36.112 --> 00:02:42.564
He drew on street stones with chalk or with charcoal on a scrap of wood.

26
00:02:42.565 --> 00:02:51.809
He drew the cathedral spire at sunset and the morning mist on the fields, whatever he saw around him.

27
00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:57.000
Because Nello lived in poverty, he did not go to school.

28
00:02:57.001 --> 00:03:03.041
Nobody paid him much attention, except Jehan and Patrasche.

29
00:03:03.042 --> 00:03:11.942
But not even they─not even Nello himself─realized that the boy was a genius at art.

30
00:03:11.943 --> 00:03:17.220
Many times from his bed at night, Jehan would say,

31
00:03:17.221 --> 00:03:30.004
"Nello, when you grow up, I hope you'll own this hut and the garden, and be called 'master' by your neighbors."

32
00:03:30.005 --> 00:03:36.891
The old soldier had wandered over all the earth in his youth and gained nothing.

33
00:03:36.892 --> 00:03:46.062
He thought that the best fate for his grandson would be to live, grow old, and die in the same home.

34
00:03:46.063 --> 00:03:53.576
Nello dreamed of other things besides being a farmer and being respected by his neighbors.

35
00:03:53.577 --> 00:04:03.726
He said nothing to his grandfather, but as he drew the beauty around him, he dreamed of becoming an artist.

36
00:04:03.727 --> 00:04:11.601
Nello whispered his dreams to Patrasche when they walked into town at daybreak every morning.

37
00:04:11.602 --> 00:04:16.095
Patrasche looked up at Nello with loving eyes.

38
00:04:16.096 --> 00:04:20.379
He hoped Nello's dreams would come true.

39
00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:25.805
Besides Patrasche, Nello had only one other friend.

40
00:04:25.806 --> 00:04:32.370
She was pretty, little Alois Cogez, who lived at the old red mill.

41
00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:43.118
Aside from the loyal Patrasche, she was the only one who knew his dream.
